Hi @rvmourik @Kocal ,
I was wondering what the current state of this feature is and what is required to finish it.

At the moment some issues occur when implementing [https://github.com/Leaflet/Leaflet.markercluster](https://github.com/Leaflet/Leaflet.markercluster) with the current leaflet bridge.
The only possible way to add a leaflet layer with clustered markers at the moment is via javascript.
This feels like unnecessary iterations over every marker in your stimulus controller.

`import { Controller } from "@hotwired/stimulus";

/* stimulusFetch: 'lazy' */
export default class extends Controller {
    connect() {
        this.element.addEventListener('ux:map:connect', this._onConnect);
    }

    disconnect() {
        this.element.removeEventListener('ux:map:connect', this._onConnect);
    }

    async _onConnect(event) {
      await import("leaflet.markercluster/dist/leaflet.markercluster-src.js");

      const { map } = event.detail;

      var clusterMarkerLayer = L.markerClusterGroup({
        spiderfyOnMaxZoom: true,
        showCoverageOnHover: false,
        zoomToBoundsOnClick: true
      });

      map.eachLayer(layer => {
        if (!(layer instanceof L.Marker)) {
            return;
        }

        clusterMarkerLayer.addLayer(layer);
        map.removeLayer(layer);
      })

      map.addLayer(clusterMarkerLayer);
    }
}`

An issue which occurs is Events are not persisted when creating a marker on this different layer.
Would the following changes suffice to resolve this?
- Implementation of a Layers object within the Map object or a reference in the Marker object.
- Changing the `doCreateMarker` in `map_controller.js` to add a marker to a configured layer or as a layer to the map.

I would like to hear your opinion on this matter.

